# Build outputs
/target
/fuzz/target
/dist

# Local/air-gapped cargo configuration (template: .cargo/config.toml.example)
/.cargo/config.toml
# Vendored crates for offline builds (docs/BUILD.md); travel as a tarball.
/third_party/cargo-vendor

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace ships binaries and builds must be
# reproducible. It must be generated against crates.io or the internal mirror;
# a lock generated with [patch] to local paths (e.g. the dev sandbox's
# offline-cargo.sh) must never be committed. CI enforces this
# (scripts/ci-check-lockfile.py).

# cargo-cyclonedx writes SBOMs next to each manifest; scripts/sbom.sh collects them.
*.cdx.json
*.cdx.xml
